# What the Quick Look preview provider needs from outside Hammerspoon, declared beside the only
# file in this spoon that opens the native panel.
# Format is name | kind | locator | policy | reason.
# See Olm's lib/deps.lua for the kinds and for how these files are found.
# Name a tool only, never how to install it. That belongs to the layer above.
#
# The compiler rather than qlmanage, and that swap is the whole story of this provider. The
# command line tool is on every Mac and it opens no window, measured rather than suspected, so
# the panel is built by a small Swift helper beside this file and the compiler is what that
# needs. Nothing here runs qlmanage any more. thumbs.lua still does and declares it for itself.
#
# The system kind, a binary at a fixed absolute path rather than something found on PATH, so the
# locator here is the path and quicklook.lua is allowed to hold that same literal. Nothing is
# injected because nothing can move it.
#
# Optional, because this is one of two preview providers and the other needs nothing. Without it
# the provider reports itself unavailable, the root falls back to the side panel, and the picker
# is exactly what it is with the panel chosen.
swiftc | system | /usr/bin/swiftc | optional | compiling the helper that opens the native Quick Look panel
